<title>UK: NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel strong.</title>
<headline>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel strong.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE straight-run fuel oil was strong again on Friday amid a scarcity of fuel, traders said.</p>
<p>An NWE refiner was heard to have bought a North Sea low sulphur cargo at or slightly above $109 a tonne fob NWE, a couple of dollars above the level of business earlier in the week.</p>
<p>High sulphur Russian cargoes were scarce, and E-4 premiums were pegged at a healthy $7-$8 over the mean/mean/mean of published quotes.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
